          "content": "**Help! I'm getting an error.**\n\nReview the [Troubleshooting](/docs/ide/troubleshooting) section for help with technical issues. Additionally, use the\n[IBM Bob community forum](https://community.ibm.com/community/user/groups/community-home?CommunityKey=300ac388-08f0-427e-a600-0199bfc9dd2a).\n\n**Bob isn't responding. What should I do?**\n\n- Check if you've exhausted your monthly Bobcoin allocation. View your balance in the gauge component (top-right corner of Bob panel) or in Settings → General tab.\n- If you're on a Pro, Pro+, or Ultra plan and have run out of Bobcoins, you can enable the [overage system](/docs/ide/account/bobcoins#overage) on the [Bob Administration](https://bob.ibm.com/admin) page to continue using Bob immediately.\n- Check if your plan has expired. You need to have a valid plan to use Bob.\n- Check your internet connection.\n- Try restarting Bob.\n\n**My Bob panel is in the wrong place. How do I move it?**\n\nYou can reposition the panel by dragging it to a new location. \n\nFor more information, see [Repositioning the Bob panel](/docs/ide/troubleshooting/ts-panel-position).\n\n**Bob made changes I didn't want. How do I undo them?**\n\nRemember to continue to use good source control practices, such as committing small, related changes frequently, and using logical branching strategies. \nYou can use the **undo** command (`Ctrl+Z` / `⌘+Z`) to revert changes. You can also use rollback to revert changes made to a file. \n\nFor more information, see [Rollback](/docs/ide/features/rollback).",
